              "inputTokens": 2448,
              "outputTokens": 411
            },
            "providerContent": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is designed for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, providing approve/reject/request-info recommendations with reasons for human admin review. The agent operates with graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, while web sources can hold a decision back but never approve independently.\n\n**Performance Results (Offline Evals):**\n- Tested on 31 cases using a local 9B model\n- Approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations\n- Fraud approved without human review dropped from 27% to 0%\n- Claude Haiku 5.5 was selected for deployment, achieving 86% accuracy vs 71%, with only 1% of fraud approved (vs 8%)\n\n**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, PostgreSQL, GCP"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
